athrm{N}, \\text { dialkyl } \\\\ \\text { acetamide }\\end{array}}{R_2 \\mathrm{NCO} \\cdot \\mathrm{CH}_3}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2019","_marksId":"67921e561d5b5072da5ea23d"},{"id":52630,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Carbylamine test is performed in alcholic KOH by heating a mixture of","options":["chloroform and silver powder","trihalogenated methane and a primary amine","an alkyl halide and a primary amine","an alkyl cyanide and a primary amine"],"answer":1,"solution":"Carbylamine test is performed in alcoholic KOH by heating a mixture of trihalogenated methane and a primary amine.\n$\\mathrm{RNH}_2 (primary \\quad anime)+\\mathrm{CHCl}_2 (chloroform) +3 \\mathrm{KOH}$ (alc.) $\\xrightarrow{\\Delta}R \\mathrm{NC} (Alkyl \\quad isocyanide) +3 \\mathrm{KCl}+3 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2017","_marksId":"67921e2a1d5b5072da5ea0dd"},{"id":52631,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Which of the following reactions is given by only primary amines?","options":["Reaction with $\\mathrm{HNO}_2$","Reaction with chloroform and alcoholic KOH","Reaction with acetyl chloride","Reaction with Grignard reagent"],"answer":1,"solution":"When a primary amine reacts with chloroform in presence of alco. KOH , it gives iso-cyanide which has abnoxious odour. This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction and it is given only by primary amines.<br/>$\\begin{aligned} \\underset{\\text { primary amine }}{\\mathrm{RHN}_2}+\\mathrm{CHCl}_3+\\underset{\\text { alco. }}{3 \\mathrm{KOH} \\xrightarrow{\\Delta}} \n\\mathrm{RNC}+3 \\mathrm{KCl}+3 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"Manipal (MET) 2011","_marksId":"67921d951d5b5072da5e9c47"},{"id":52632,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Which one of the following compounds will dissolve in an alkali solution after it has undergone reaction with Hinsberg reagent?","options":["$\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{NH}_2$","$\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{~N}$","$\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_5\\right)_2 \\mathrm{NH}$","$\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{NHC}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5$"],"answer":0,"solution":"$\\underset{1^{\\circ} \\text { amine }}{\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{NH}_2}+\\underset{\\substack{\\text { Hinsberg's } \\\\ \\text { reagent }}}{\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{SO}_2 \\mathrm{Cl}} \\longrightarrow \\underset{\\substack{\\text { N-methyl benzene } \\\\ \\text { sulphonamide }}}{\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{SO}_2 \\mathrm{NHCH}_3} \\xrightarrow[\\text { (alkali) }]{\\mathrm{NaOH}} \\underset{\\text { soluble sodium salt }}{\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5 \\mathrm{SO}_2 \\mathrm{~N}(\\mathrm{Na}) \\mathrm{CH}_3}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2010","_marksId":"67921d761d5b5072da5e9b46"}]}